From 967d7fb65498503ea280edc5843d2366554ec984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:42:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] MSL: geometry shaders through object/mesh stages: every
 input topology, output topology, builtins

- The object stage groups the draw's vertexes into the geometry shader's input
  primitives at run time, by the VkPrimitiveTopology in DrawInfo: lists, strips
  (odd triangles in Vulkan's order) and fans, and lines and triangles with
  adjacency (lists and strips). input_primitive_type now only sets the
  vertexes per primitive (points, lines, triangles, with adjacency).
- gl_PrimitiveIDIn (passed in the payload) and gl_InvocationID; instanced
  geometry shaders (geometry_invocations mesh threadgroups per primitive).
- The mesh topology and primitive count follow the output primitive (points,
  line strips, triangle strips); odd triangles of a strip keep the winding.
- Point size follows the geometry shader's output primitive.
- Geometry shaders without inputs, and with only the mesh output parameter.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 158 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 spirv_msl.hpp |   9 ++-
 2 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

